  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Dropping and immediately picking up an object twice within a single physics time step will result in the bounciness parameter of all colliders within the pickup object being permanently reduced to 0. The result of this is that objects which are normally expected to bounce will simply slide across any surface they hit.\n\nThis bug can be easily reproduced in VR simply by picking up and dropping the same object several times in quick succession using both hands.",
